# 2026-03-23: Pipeline Designer, undo/redo, auto-save, dark mode, conversational errors,
#             URL routing, security views wired to backend, API proxy, PostgreSQL running.
# 2026-04-03: Stack trace exposure fixed in rokur/main.js and vordr/http-server.ts.
#             Error details now logged server-side only, removed from HTTP responses.
# 2026-04-04: CRG D→C blitz. Added: selur property_test.rs (18 proptest), e2e_test.rs (10),
#             aspect_test.rs (13); vordr property_test.rs (15 proptest), e2e_test.rs (7).
#             Deno: unit/container_types_test.ts (27), property/nickel_config_properties_test.ts (20),
#             e2e/container_lifecycle_test.ts (7), aspect/security_test.ts (10).
#             Fixed both vordr benchmarks (container_lifecycle + ebpf_overhead — pre-existing API errors).
#             Removed tests/fuzz/placeholder.txt. All tests pass: 186+80 Deno + 48 new Rust = 314+ total.
# 2026-04-04: Session 9 dogfooding. Added: tests/property/layer_invariants_test.ts (25 property tests),
#             .github/workflows/e2e.yml workflow. Completion 87% → 91% (4% for property + test infrastructure).
# 2026-04-19: Idris2 proof build restored in cerro-torre/verification/idris. After the assert_total
#             spec-stub removal the modules had stopped type-checking: `chainCommutative` had a real
#             type error, and five other proofs (verifyChain, chainHeadValid, chainTailValid,
#             chainImpliesIndividual, chainExtension + their callers in Theorems.idr) were flagged
#             "not covering" under %default total because they transitively call the partial
#             `verifyEd25519`/`sha256`/string-primitive spec stubs. Fixes:
#               - Propagated explicit `partial` markers through every caller of a spec stub so
#                 partiality stays auditable without disabling %default total.
#               - Disambiguated Data.List.isPrefixOf vs Data.String.isPrefixOf in SafePath and
#                 normalizedIsSafe; added Data.Nat + Decidable.Equality imports.
#               - Added Eq TarEntry so OCILayout's hasManifest `elem` witness type-checks.
#               - Hoisted TarEntry above its first use (was declared after the postulates that
#                 referred to it); fixed the `size`-shadow warning in tarBombPrevention.
#               - Theorems.idr: added Data.Vect import (was leaning on transitive visibility);
#                 marked computeBundleHash / WellFormed / ProperlySigned / bundleIntegrity /
#                 signatureChainSoundness / supplyChainIntegrity / thresholdSatisfaction /
#                 nonRepudiation as partial (inherited from spec stubs).
#               - `chainCommutative`: demoted from proven to postulate. The with-block proof
#                 fails because Idris2's with-abstraction is syntactic — the goal
#                 `verifyChain hash [a,b] = verifyChain hash [b,a]` never contains
#                 `verifyEd25519 ...` as a literal subterm at abstraction time, and Idris2 refuses
#                 to reduce `verifyChain [n]` past an opaque verifyEd25519 head. Documented the
#                 required refactor (`verifyChain = allValid ∘ map verifyPair` with pattern-match
#                 on Bool head) in the postulate comment + PROOF-NEEDS.md §"chainCommutative
#                 regression". Postulate count 12 → 13 (regression acknowledged, not hidden).
#             Net: all 5 modules now build clean under %default total with zero warnings.
